{"metadata":{"description":"dsh-agent-team: Agent Teams for DeepSeek Harness. Hand work to a team of agents that carries it end to end while you set the direction and hold the gates. You stay on the loop, and step back in whenever you want.","id":"gh:1343951443","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-agent-team","slug":"Contexera/dsh-agent-team","topics":["agent-orchestration","agent-team","ai-agents","ai-teammates","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","human-on-the-loop","multi-agent","multi-agent-systems"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh-agent-team: Agent Teams for DeepSeek Harness. Hand work to a team of agents that carries it end "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"to end while you set the direction and hold the gates. You stay on the loop, and step back in whenev"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" you set the direction and hold the gates. You stay on the loop, and step back in whenever you want."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-agent-team — Agent Teams for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Hand work to a team of agents: they carry it end to end while you set the direction and hold the g"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"work to a team of agents: they carry it end to end while you set the direction and hold the gates.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"An opt-in plugin for DeepSeek Harness: install it only where Team mode is needed; ordinary DSH sessi"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ons keep their normal preset roster."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## In the loop, or on the loop"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"With a coding agent you are *in* the loop: you ask, read, correct, and ask again. That is the right "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"way to drive work you want to hold yourself. It stops scaling once there are several agents. You bec"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"ome their dispatcher, their reviewer, and their memory, and every line of work waits on you."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"dsh-agent-team puts you *on* the loop. Agents claim Tasks, hand work to each other, and have someone"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" other than the builder verify it. They come back to you for what stays yours: the direction, the tr"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ust, and the step that cannot be undone. Both ways of working live side by side in the same DSH."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## How we use it"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"This repository is built by its own team: one Human and a group of Agents, split across Projects for"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" development, bug fixing, UI, review, evaluation, and release. In one bug-fix line, an Agent owner f"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ound a defect while checking the live Web UI, scoped it, handed it to another Agent, re-ran every ga"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"te itself, and accepted the result. The Human never had to post in that Thread."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Why you can step back"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- **Members persist.** Each agent is a named Member with its own memory, notes, and skills. It is th"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"e same Member after its session ends, its context is compacted or replaced, or DSH restarts, so you "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"brief it once.
- **Every outcome has one owner.** Projects have named owners, and every Task has one"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" accountable owner, Human or Agent, who drives it to acceptance.
- **Whoever builds does not verify."},{"id":"p12s5","text":"** An Agent may accept a Task only once it is in review, and only if it never held a Claim on it. Cl"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"ose, reopen, and transfer stay with the accountable owner and with you.
- **The room is built for ag"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"ents.** Agents pull from their own Inbox instead of being pushed every message, and a reply written "},{"id":"p12s8","text":"against a Thread that has moved on is refused and handed back with what changed, so the agent decide"},{"id":"p12s9","text":"s again before it speaks.
- **Everything is on the record.** The Main stream, Threads, and Tasks liv"},{"id":"p12s10","text":"e on one append-only ledger. The task board and your Inbox are views of it, so you read where the wo"},{"id":"p12s11","text":"rk stands instead of asking."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## When to hand work to the team"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Open a session yourself when you want to hold the thread: exploring, deep design, or a change you wa"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"nt to watch line by line."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Hand it to the team when any of these holds:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- the work splits into lines that can move in parallel;
- it should keep moving while you are away f"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"rom it;
- it should be verified by someone other than whoever built it;
- it recurs, and deserves a "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"standing owner: a Project."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"You can always step back in. Mention or message a Member, open its Thread, or open its own session."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Where it stands today"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- **One machine.** One DSH server, one Human, and as many Agents as you create. Several Humans shari"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ng one Team is not supported yet.
- **Agents wake on Team events.** A message, a mention, a hand-off"},{"id":"p19s3","text":", or a reminder raised by activity wakes them. There is no timer: a Team that has gone completely qu"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"iet does not wake itself, and nothing runs while the machine is off.
- **Agents work with full acces"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"s.** Managed Agent Sessions run with `danger-full-access` in their Workspace, so create Agents only "},{"id":"p19s6","text":"in a Workspace you trust."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"If this looks useful, a star on GitHub helps other DSH users find it."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### 1. Check DSH"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"This release is certified against DSH `0.2.2-rc.1`. Install the DSH version explicitly rather than f"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"ollowing `latest`: an unpinned install can resolve to a line outside the range this bundle declares."},{"id":"p23s3","text":" On DSH `0.1.7-rc.2`, stay on `@wowyuarm/dsh-agent-team` `0.1.15`. On DSH `0.2.0-rc.2`, stay on `@co"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"ntexera/dsh-agent-team` `0.2.3`. On DSH `0.2.0-rc.1`, stay on `@wowyuarm/dsh-agent-team` `0.2.0`. On"},{"id":"p23s5","text":" DSH `0.2.1-rc.x`, stay on `@contexera/dsh-agent-team` `0.2.6`."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Install it globally if you want the `dsh` command for the steps below: `npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@0."},{"id":"p25s2","text":" globally if you want the `dsh` command for the steps below: `npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-rc.1`."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Stop it, then install Agent Team into the `web` profile:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The version is pinned deliberately: pnpm skips releases published less than 24 hours ago, so an unpi"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"nned `@latest` install resolves to the previous release on release day."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"This plugin publishes as `@contexera/dsh-agent-team`, with its repository at `Contexera/dsh-agent-te"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"am`. The former `@wowyuarm/dsh-agent-team` stays at 0.2.1 and is deprecated in favour of the new nam"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"e; an existing profile swaps the plugin's name, not its data."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### 2. Start the Web UI"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## What it adds"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"- A durable single-host Team: Workspaces, Projects with a Main stream and named owners, discussion a"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"nd Task Threads, Claims, accountable owners, and a task board.
- A Web Client for the Human: create "},{"id":"p34s3","text":"Projects and Agents, set owners, post and reply, follow or step back from Threads, and accept, close"},{"id":"p34s4","text":", reopen, or transfer Tasks. The Inbox and a cross-Workspace task board show what needs you.
- An is"},{"id":"p34s5","text":"olated `team-member` preset with nine model-facing Team tools: `team_inbox`, `team_thread`, `team_at"},{"id":"p34s6","text":"tention`, `team_message`, `team_dm`, `team_task`, `team_view`, `team_subscription`, and `team_remind"},{"id":"p34s7","text":"er`.
- A pull-based collaboration protocol. Agent Inbox admission is durable, but it does not claim "},{"id":"p34s8","text":"that the model has already processed the update."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"The Team is one collaboration domain per DSH home. Its append-only operation ledger is the authority"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"; UI, Remote responses, tools, Inbox, and other projections derive from committed operations. Ordina"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"ry DSH Sessions keep the profile's normal preset roster and do not receive Team tools or guidance."}],"truncated":true}
